    "original_title": "Duqa Gaalkacyo: “Waxaan rabnaa inaan ka baxno Buntilaan iyo Galmudug”",
    "slug": "gaalkacyo-mayor-calls-for-city-to-become-self-governing",
    "summary": "The mayor of Gaalkacyo's Puntland side, Xuseen Cabdinuur Maxamed, has said the city should become self-administered and independent from both Puntland and Galmudug. His remarks come amid renewed tensions between the federal government and Puntland over the city's status.",
    "content": "The mayor of the Puntland-administered part of Gaalkacyo, Xuseen Cabdinuur Maxamed, announced on August 17 that he envisions the city becoming an autonomous municipality, free from the authority of both the Puntland and Galmudug regional administrations. In a statement, he said that in the near future, Gaalkacyo should be a self-governing city within Somalia, independent of the two federal member states.\n\nThe mayor's declaration surfaces at a time when Gaalkacyo has once again become a focal point of political friction between Somalia's federal government and Puntland. The city is uniquely divided, with parts under Puntland's control and other sections under Galmudug, a split that has historically led to administrative confusion and periodic conflict over resources and governance.\n\nHis remarks are likely to intensify debates about the city's political future. Gaalkacyo's location and economic significance make its status highly sensitive, as both Puntland and Galmudug claim influence over it. The call for self-governance could be interpreted as a response to the broader challenges of managing a divided city amid national political tensions.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, many of whom trace their roots to Gaalkacyo or have business interests there, this development carries potential implications for stability and investment. A push for autonomy may alter the political landscape, affecting everything from security arrangements to local governance and economic opportunities. The diaspora community will be watching closely to see whether this proposal gains traction or remains a symbolic stance.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/08/17/duqa-gaalkacyo-waxaan-rabnaa-inaan-ka-baxno-buntilaan-iyo-galmudug/",
