    "content": "On August 16, 2026, President Hassan Sheikh Mohamud, in his capacity as Commander-in-Chief of the Somali Armed Forces, officially graduated thousands of soldiers from the Xananbuure training camp in the Galguduud region. The soldiers had completed nearly a year of intensive military training, preparing them for deployment in national security operations.\n\nThis graduation event is particularly significant as it represents the largest single cohort of soldiers to complete training inside Somalia since the fall of the central government in 1991. The training program at Xananbuure is part of a broader national strategy to rebuild the Somali military and enhance its capacity to ensure security without excessive reliance on foreign forces.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, this development signals a step toward greater national sovereignty and stability. A stronger, home-trained military may reduce the need for external military interventions, potentially fostering conditions that enable diaspora investment and eventual return. The progress in military capacity also reflects ongoing efforts to strengthen state institutions after decades of conflict.\n\nRead the original report from Radio Dalsan here: https://radiodalsan.com/2026/08/16/president-hassan-sheikh-graduates-thousands-of-soldiers-in-xananbuure/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=president-hassan-sheikh-graduates-thousands-of-soldiers-in-xananbuure",
